# Mode projection of an MD trajectory (crystod-md --project); testsuite
# section 40
# Every frame is matched to the ideal supercell of the parent primitive cell
# (-c, --dim; by element and nearest image of the time-averaged positions, so
# the atom order of the XDATCAR does not matter), the mass-weighted
# centre-of-mass displacement of every frame is removed (drift), and the
# displacements are projected onto the symmetry-adapted patterns of
# crystod-phonon --vibration (ISO-IR labels, mode-space and component numbers
# as there for a parent in the standard setting). Q = p_hat . u / sqrt(N):
# the displacement norm per parent primitive cell carried by the pattern, at
# a time-reversal invariant q the amplitude of crystod-phonon --modulation
# (elsewhere a frozen amplitude A gives A/sqrt(2) over the c/s components);
# the AMPLIMODES amplitude of an irrep in crystod-group --supergroup-cif is
# sqrt(size) times the norm of its Q over all components and arms (Q
# sqrt(size) for a single component).
# Files: MDPROJ_<formula>_<q>.csv (step = XDATCAR configuration number, then
# one column per component, label_space_component), MDPROJ_<formula>_hist.pdf
# (histograms with Gaussian reference lines; --no-histogram skips it),
# MDPROJ_<formula>.npz with --npz; -o PREFIX renames them.
# With --yaml phonopy_params.yaml the basis is the phonon eigenvectors at each
# q (sections 5-7 and 9): default prefix MDPROJ_<formula>_phonon, columns
# <mode>_<irrep>, npz arrays a_<q> and frequencies_<q>.
# XDATCAR_synthetic and XDATCAR_I4mcm_1 are written by make_xdatcar.py.

# (1) Synthetic 2x2x2 ScF3 trajectory: R4+ component 1 frozen as
# 0.3 sin(2 pi t/50) A and M3+ at M (1/2, 1/2, 0) as 0.17 cos(2 pi t/37) A
# (100 frames, atoms shuffled). Both come back exactly (CSV columns); a
# sinusoid has ratio 2 sqrt(2)/pi = 0.900 and kurtosis -1.5, and its
# histogram two peaks at the turning points. The pooled R4+ row reads
# "unequal" (one moving and two zero components are not one distribution).
# The sum rule confirms that the two patterns carry all of the displacement.

$ crystod-md --project -c ../test_POSCARs/221_PPOSCAR_ScF3 --dim 2 2 2 --xdatcar XDATCAR_synthetic --qpoint R M --irrep R4+ M3+

* Input *
  Parent cell     : ../test_POSCARs/221_PPOSCAR_ScF3
  Space group     : Pm-3m (No. 221)
  Supercell (dim) : 2 2 2 (8 parent cells, 32 atoms)
  Trajectory      : XDATCAR_synthetic (100 frames)
  Frames used     : 100 (step 0 .. 99; configuration 1 .. 100)
  Lattice         : fixed cell

* Site matching *
  Sites matched   : 32 (one-to-one, by element and nearest image
                    of the time-averaged position)
  Uniform shift   : (+0.0000, +0.0000, +0.0000) A (mean offset of the averaged structure)
  Largest offset  : 0.0060 A (atom 11, uniform shift removed)
  Drift           : the mass-weighted centre-of-mass displacement is removed
                    from every frame (rms 0.0000 A)

* Q points *
  R        (1/2, 1/2, 1/2)
  M        (1/2, 1/2, 0)

* Mode projection at R (1/2, 1/2, 1/2) *
irrep   space  component  <Q> (A)  sqrt<Q^2> (A)  <|Q|> (A)  ratio  kurtosis  n_eff  shape
R4+(3)  3      1          0.00000  0.21213        0.19073    0.899  -1.50     6      double-peaked (hint)
R4+(3)  3      2          0.00000  0.00000        0.00000    -      -         -      zero
R4+(3)  3      3          0.00000  0.00000        0.00000    -      -         -      zero

* Pooled components and norm |Q| at R (1/2, 1/2, 1/2) *
irrep   space  comps  sqrt<Q^2> (A)  ratio  kurtosis  n_eff  shape    <|Q|> (A)  |Q| ratio  Gaussian
R4+(3)  3      3      0.12247        -      -         -      unequal  0.19073    0.899      0.921

* Mode projection at M (1/2, 1/2, 0) *
irrep   space  component  <Q> (A)   sqrt<Q^2> (A)  <|Q|> (A)  ratio  kurtosis  n_eff  shape
M3+(1)  2      1          -0.00845  0.12173        0.11029    0.906  -1.51     9      double-peaked (hint)

* Sum rule *
  sum of <Q^2> over the projected components : 0.059818 A^2
  <|u|^2> / N (all atoms, drift removed)     : 0.059818 A^2
  fraction covered                           : 100.00 %
  q points covered                           : 2 of 8 commensurate (a -q partner counts with its q)

* Notes *
  Q: displacement norm per parent primitive cell carried by the pattern; at a
     time-reversal invariant q it equals the crystod-phonon --modulation amplitude,
     elsewhere --amplitude A gives a norm of A/sqrt(2) over its c/s components.
  AMPLIMODES amplitude of an irrep = sqrt(size) x the norm of its Q over all
     components and arms (Q sqrt(size) for a single component).
  ratio = <|Q|>/sqrt<Q^2>: 0.798 for a Gaussian about Q = 0 (single well,
     displacive), 1 for two states +-Q0 (order-disorder).
  shape: histogram density at Q = 0 against its maximum (< 0.5 with weight on
     both sides: double-peaked); a hint from the statistics, not a test.
  n_eff: frames / autocorrelation time; ratio and kurtosis scatter ~ 1/sqrt(n_eff).
  Pooled: all components of a mode space as one sample (equivalent components
     in the parent symmetry); unequal: component rms values differ by more than
     a factor 3 (no pooled shape); |Q| ratio = <|Q|>/sqrt<|Q|^2>,
     Gaussian = its value for an isotropic Gaussian in that many components.
  Components 1c/1s: the real patterns of a complex row e and of i e (q not
     time-reversal invariant; -q gives the same patterns).

* Output files *
  MDPROJ_ScF3_R.csv
  MDPROJ_ScF3_M.csv
  MDPROJ_ScF3_hist.pdf


