# (4) Every commensurate q (64 for 4x4x4; q and -q share their real patterns,
# so 36 are projected): the sum rule is exact. <|u|^2>/N = 0.2263 A^2 per
# cell; --adp (../39_xdatcar2adp) gives 3 (U_eq(Sc) + 3 U_eq(F)) =
# 3 (0.005477 + 3 x 0.023486) = 0.2278 A^2 (ratio 0.993). The difference:
# --adp measures each atom about its own time-averaged position (the static
# offsets of the averaged structure from the ideal sites, 0.0012 A^2 per
# cell here, are left out) and converts all frames with the cell of the
# first analysed frame (0.4 % longer than the mean cell; with that cell the
# projection gives 0.2293 - 0.0013 = 0.2281 A^2), while --project uses each
# frame's own cell (--mean-lattice: the mean cell, 0.2271 A^2) and removes
# the centre-of-mass drift of every frame.

$ crystod-md --project -c ../test_POSCARs/221_PPOSCAR_ScF3 --dim 4 4 4 --xdatcar ../39_xdatcar2adp/ScF3_Pm-3m_NpT_300K/XDATCAR_every10 --start-step 0 --qpoint all --no-histogram -o all/MDPROJ_ScF3_300K

