  MDPROJ_I4mcm_1_phonon_R.csv


# (6) The NpT run of (3) with effective frequencies (--temperature 300):
# nu_eff = sqrt(k_B T/<a^2>)/(2 pi), the frequency of the harmonic oscillator
# with the same <a^2> at T (classical equipartition, equilibrated run). The
# stiff F-dominated modes above 10 THz follow the harmonic model (every mode
# within 21 %, the pooled levels within 11 %), and so do R5+, M5-, GM5- and
# GM4- within a few per cent; the acoustic GM4- modes carry nothing after the
# centre-of-mass removal; the M3+ tilt is harmonic (1.698 against 1.670 THz);
# the R4+ tilts fluctuate more than the harmonic model predicts (pooled nu_eff
# 0.744 against 1.417 THz). The run and the yaml do not share a reference
# (mean cell 4.038 against 4.0696 A, a different energy model; kinetic
# temperature std 72 K against about 15 K for a canonical ensemble), so this
# comparison says nothing about anharmonic stabilization. The lower M3- mode
# (9.272 against 3.974 THz) belongs to an irrep that occurs twice at M (see
# the crystod-md page of the CrystOD manual).
# (The CSV files of this run are not kept here.)

$ crystod-md --project --yaml ../33_modulation/ScF3_Pm-3m/phonopy_params.yaml --dim 4 4 4 --xdatcar ../39_xdatcar2adp/ScF3_Pm-3m_NpT_300K/XDATCAR_every10 --start-step 0 --qpoint R M GM --temperature 300 -o MDPROJ_ScF3_300K_phonon

